    "question": {
      ":question/id": "ffca1833-5d5d-5660-9bf5-bd2dcb5ca9f0",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $U$ into the matrix $V$, where\n\n$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nV=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that the $1$st row is the same in both matrices. The only rows that have changed are the $3$rd row and the $2$nd row.   \n\nBy considering the given row operations that change both the $3$rd and the $2$nd row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & \\,{R}_{3}\u2194{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =V.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}\u2194{R}_{2}.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
