      ":question/problem": "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $K$ into the matrix $L$, where\n\n$$\nK=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that the $2$nd and $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $1$st row.\n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $1$st row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}K & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{3} \\\\ & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ & =L.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{3}.\n$$",
